<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38611" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεμ-βάτης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one mounted,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππων ἐπεμβάται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					782
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i>horseman,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				75.6
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁρμάτων ἐ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					585
				</span></i>
			: abs., ib.<i><span class="en">
				685
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>one who walks on</i> or <i>in,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπεμβάται ἴχνεσι κούφοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Orph.
					<u>H.</u>
					31.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
